  "findings": [
    "Two predicted-paper points recover the hand-held printed checker and foliage checker, but lose aircraft and red/white ribbon checker. Proposal count remains 14/22.",
    "Known-paper false negatives fall from 2.47% to 0.43%, but mean known-background false positives rise from 6.56% to 6.76%. Mean known-region IoU changes from 90.70% to 91.37%.",
    "On the ribbon checker (real-c0cc1ce97cf5e6a6), one automatically chosen paper point is visibly on the blue background. The original body field falsely includes that region, so a colour-specific deepest-point rule amplifies an upstream segmentation mistake.",
    "The hand-held printed checker now includes both papers; the blue/yellow checker also includes both, but retains too much background and still produces no crop.",
    "No full fitting replay was run for the two-paper arm. No policy chooses the better arm per photograph, and the union of their outcomes is not claimed as a validated algorithm."
  ],
  "nextStep": "Test a constrained prompt fallback and isolate locator shape/colour losses on accurate silhouettes; verify complete templates before integration.",
